WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.296
Major arcana XV to XVIII cover attachment,
upheaval, hope and uncertainty.

00:00:06.296 --> 00:00:11.185
Here is what each tarot card traditionally
means, upright and reversed.

00:00:12.485 --> 00:00:13.094
The Devil.

00:00:13.094 --> 00:00:17.421
Two small figures are chained loosely to a
horned figure on a pedestal.

00:00:17.421 --> 00:00:20.589
Attachment, constraint, temptation, the
shadow side.

00:00:21.889 --> 00:00:22.533
The Tower.

00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:26.204
Lightning strikes a tall tower, and
figures fall from it.

00:00:26.204 --> 00:00:30.004
Upheaval, sudden change, revelation,
structures giving way.

00:00:31.304 --> 00:00:31.877
The Star.

00:00:31.877 --> 00:00:39.512
A figure kneels at a pool, pouring water onto the land and into
the pool, under a large star surrounded by smaller ones.

00:00:40.912 --> 00:00:43.289
Have a tarot spread in front of you?

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:48.110
Photograph it at readmyspread.com, and get
a clear reading, card by card.
